      "body": "### Summary\n\nThis PR updates the catalog for JSP-000936 (Erdős Problem #1128 / #1129: Which Lagrange interpolation nodes minimize the maximum amplification of input errors?) to indicate that a formal proof in Lean 4 has been completed.\n\n- Standalone formalization & DefEq bridge repository: https://github.com/Drag0ndddd1118/jsp-000936-formalization\n- Mathematical resolution: Resolved by Carl de Boor and Allan Pinkus (1978), confirming Bernstein and Erdős's conjectures regarding the existence and non-uniqueness of optimal node systems.\n- Axioms: Standard Lean foundation `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` (0 custom axioms, 0 sorry, 0 admit)\n- Verification: Complete GitHub Actions CI green & automated double-checked with `check.py`\n\nLinks to prior catalog submissions: none",
